Add batched DB cleanup to prevent InnoDB buffer pool exhaustion

Backport of upstream commit a28ddb94c3 (master, 2026-06-03, Change-Id
I58e6efbe81293b8943cc41d6c47f6a52264f376c). Barbican 23.0.0 contains
it, 22.0.0 does not, no 22.0.x tag exists that could be pinned instead,
and stable/2026.1 does not carry it.

Barbican 22.0.0 runs the whole of `barbican-manage db clean` in one
transaction: `clean_command` (barbican/model/clean.py) calls
`repo.commit()` once, after the last table. The statements filter on
`deleted`, `deleted_at` and `expiration`, which no index covers, so
each one reads its whole table and locks what it reads. The pass that
soft-deletes expired secrets selects the matching rows first
(`synchronize_session='fetch'`) and updates them afterwards. A secret
the API commits between the two fails the update with MariaDB error
1020 ("Record has changed since last read"; MariaDB 12.3 with
innodb_snapshot_isolation=ON under REPEATABLE READ), and the rollback
discards the whole run. Measured on 2026-11-13 against MariaDB 12.3.3,
the published 2026.1 image failed 13 of 13 runs under concurrent API
writes, each with 1020 on `secrets`; in the C5C3/playground cluster all
seven attempts of the clean-up Job of 2026-11-12 failed the same way.

The upstream commit selects up to 10,000 ids with a plain read, changes
those rows by primary key and commits after every batch, so a failed
run keeps the batches it committed and the next run continues behind
them. The cherry-pick applies to 22.0.0 without a conflict, and the
three files it touches then equal their 23.0.0 versions byte for byte.
The batched code also lets the retry patch that follows apply to both
releases unchanged.

The backport gives the legacy `barbican-db-manage` entry point a
`--batch-size` option (barbican/cmd/db_manage.py).
`barbican-manage db clean`, the command the barbican-operator runs,
takes none and runs with `DEFAULT_CLEANUP_BATCH_SIZE = 10000`.

Tests: the upstream test hunks (barbican/tests/cmd/test_db_cleanup.py)
travel inside the patch unchanged; no other upstream test pins the
single transaction.

Proof: tests/container-images/verify_barbican.sh (Test 9) asserts in
the built image that a clean-up batch is committed on its own; without
this backport no commit happens per batch.

No 2026.2 twin: 23.0.0 carries the commit.

Applies to barbican 22.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: merged on master as a28ddb94c3 (2026-06-03,
Closes-bug: #2155108), not backported to stable/2026.1.

